# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository and check them out with the
# platform's native line ending. The engine writes output using native line
# endings (CRLF on Windows, LF on Unix), and the golden-file tests compare the
# engine's output byte-for-byte against the checked-in *.output.expected files,
# so those fixtures must also be checked out with native endings on each
# platform. `text=auto` guarantees this regardless of a user's core.autocrlf.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must stay LF even when checked out on Windows (a CRLF shebang
# line breaks them on Unix); Windows batch files should be CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# The prebuilt Linux engine is a binary — never apply text/EOL conversion.
bin/bbpPairings binary

